                    coach_r3_thinreinforce: `<strong>Reinforcement is under-funded.</strong> A little manager briefing is better than none, but the pilot's 9% follow-up is the warning. Staff return to branches that pull them back to counting cash unless managers actively coach the new behaviour.`,
                    coach_r3_noreinforce:   `<strong>You spent it all on content and trainers and nothing on the managers.</strong> In the pilot 9% of managers followed up and transfer was 11%. Without reinforcement your staff return to branches that pull them straight back. Where is the money that makes managers coach this?`,
                    coach_r3_prestige:      `<strong>Prestige trainers just blew the cap.</strong> External experts at scale push you over €792/learner with nothing left for reinforcement. Trained internal coaches have more contextual credibility for a third of the cost — what did the prestige actually buy?`,
                    coach_r4_fourlevel:     `<strong>You're measuring all four Kirkpatrick levels.</strong> Reaction (and usefulness, not just enjoyment), learning, on-the-job behaviour and advisory revenue. That's what tells the CFO whether 2,400 people changed and sold — not whether they liked it.`,
